  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Remodel framing can sometimes feel like a puzzle, but avoiding common mistakes can keep your project on schedule. Here are a few things to watch out for:"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "1. Starting before the final layout is confirmed: This is a big one! Making changes after framing has begun leads to costly rework and wasted time. Make sure you’re completely happy with the design before the first stud goes up."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "2. Ordering materials too late: Don’t wait until the last minute to order your lumber and other framing materials. Supply chain issues can cause unexpected delays, so plan ahead."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4,
      "name": "Step 4",
      "text": "3. Failing to coordinate with other trades: Framing impacts everything else – plumbing, electrical, HVAC. Ensure everyone is on the same page and their work is properly sequenced."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5,
      "name": "Step 5",
      "text": "4. Not factoring in inspection times: Inspections for framing, sheathing, and fire-blocking are mandatory before you can close up walls. These can take anywhere from 2-10 business days per cycle, depending on your local jurisdiction. Don't forget to schedule them!"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6,
      "name": "Step 6",
      "text": "5. Overlooking structural changes: If your remodel involves altering load paths or adding new openings, you'll likely need a licensed contractor and possibly a structural engineer. Skipping this step can lead to safety issues and failed inspections."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 7,
      "name": "Step 7",
      "text": "By keeping these points in mind, you can help ensure your remodel framing project goes as smoothly as possible. Need a hand with your project? We're here to help!"
    }
  ],
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
